  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-23T20:23:21.836Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In this time of quarantine, it is much harder for people to meet up physically, especially in the academics. Now, with the coming advent of the new age of online learning, I propose that Vr chat partner with colleges to provide an online learning space. This could be implemented via private rooms tailored to allow outside links, videos, draw pens, etc. This, along with perhaps creating a system to upload pdfs or other word-esque documents to allow for access of scholarly texts, I believe would be an interesting spin on how we learn. Why not have a virtual classroom that is literally a classroom? This is by no means an easy or simple matter in execution, but one that is certainly possible, perhaps even profitable, both in the name of creativity, social activity, learnitivity and any other positive words that end in -ity that would be a positive descriptor of this proposed form of alternative avenue for online learning. Thank you for your time and feel free to post your critiques, approvals, or any other thoughts you may have on such a matter. Have a nice day, and maybe one day we can see elmo and shrek get a lesson on the Homestead Act from Professor Layton. Honestly though, I would be happy if there was a dedicated tab for reading downloaded books while in chill rooms.",
